    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "SBh6N",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "note 00 · Onboarding",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "00 · ONBOARDING\n• Six local steps: language and theme → controllers → game folders → runtime core → terms of use → summary.\n• Every step must be completable with a controller. Keyboard and mouse input are supplementary.\n• The BYOR/BYOC step states what AYTHER supplies and what the user must provide. Acceptance records the terms version and date.\n• A runtime core is validated outside the launcher process before it is saved. Architecture or platform mismatches produce an actionable error rather than a runtime crash.\n• Online accounts and remote-service setup are outside the CE onboarding flow.\n• Configuration is written atomically only after completion. An interrupted wizard resumes at the last incomplete step."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "7ezhH",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 1400,
      "name": "note 01 · Home",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "01 · HOME\n• Continue launches the most recently played game with its selected local profile and latest compatible save.\n• Pass a stable game identifier to the launch path, never a list index that changes across filtered, recent, and hero models.\n• Do not show a hero when no game has been played. Distinguish an empty library from a populated library with no play history.\n• Recent games exclude the hero entry and hidden games.\n• Play time comes from the local session record and is accumulated even after an unclean exit. Display rounded, human-readable durations rather than a running seconds counter.\n• Home, Library, and Settings are the only primary sections. Vertical navigation remains inside the page; section changes use the dedicated previous/next-section controls."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "sKhtA",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 2800,
      "name": "note 02 · Library",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "02 · LIBRARY\n• The cover grid is the default view; the list is an alternative. Both preserve an obvious focus ring and remain fully navigable by controller.\n• Column count derives from available width. Vertical movement follows rows, horizontal movement traverses the complete collection, and focus scrolling keeps the selected game visible.\n• Scanning is incremental, cancellable, and non-blocking. Cancellation keeps verified results and never prunes folders that were not reached. Cache writes use a temporary file followed by an atomic rename.\n• Compatibility uses one validator and four stable grades across cards, lists, and details. Status always combines text, icon, and color, with an actionable explanation for the selected game.\n• Local cover art takes precedence; otherwise use a platform-specific placeholder. Remote metadata is not required.\n• Filters are session-scoped. Favorites, hidden state, and user metadata overrides persist. Clearing an override restores the untouched detected value.\n• The selected grid/list view persists, while the available platform filters derive only from games present in the library."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "MUDkg",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 4200,
      "name": "note 03 · Game details",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "03 · GAME DETAILS\n• The game is the subject of the page. Pack information is one local row, not a separate remote listing.\n• Controller actions remain visible beside their labels: Continue or Play, Original or enhanced profile, configuration, saves, and credits where available.\n• Compatibility is evaluated once and presented consistently across ROM, runtime core, and pack requirements. The most severe actionable explanation is shown first.\n• Opening the page must not synchronously reread a large pack on the UI thread. Reuse scan results and load remaining local metadata asynchronously.\n• A successful integrity check means the archive matches its own manifest; it does not establish publisher identity or safety. Use file-integrity wording and never a trust seal.\n• Continue and New Game are separate actions. Safe mode starts without a previous save or optional enhancement state.\n• Save history is versioned by game, profile, ROM revision, and timestamp. Restoring creates a new current version instead of overwriting history."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "GSB5R",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 5600,
      "name": "note 04 · Launch",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "04 · LAUNCH AND SESSION\n• Each session receives an immutable launch manifest under the local data directory. Runtime arguments derive from that manifest so the launch is reproducible and orphaned sessions can be detected.\n• Runtime status uses typed, versioned events rather than substring matching. The overlay reports real initialization stages and separates warnings from fatal errors.\n• A second launch of the same game is rejected while its session is active.\n• Saves and session metadata are written to temporary files and atomically renamed. An interrupted write must not replace the last valid state.\n• Unexpected exits preserve diagnostics and offer a safe-mode retry that removes optional pack and saved-state inputs without modifying the original game or save files.\n• Session summaries report only locally observed play time and created artifacts. No background submission is part of CE."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "M3GFX",
      "x": -880,
      "y": 7000,
      "name": "note 05 · Settings",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "05 · SETTINGS\n• Sections cover System, Video, Audio, Input, and Accessibility, with controller shortcuts between them.\n• Setting precedence is visible: global → platform → game → pack. The current value and its source appear together.\n• Game folders and runtime cores reuse the same validated dialogs as onboarding.\n• The local data directory is displayed but not edited inline because moving it is a migration operation, not a simple preference.\n• Local pack folders and install-from-disk actions belong with other content settings. Removing a configured folder never deletes its files.\n• Export remains visible because it is the primary backup path for local saves and preferences.\n• Account, cloud synchronization, telemetry, and service-managed update controls are outside CE and do not appear in this screen.\n• Destructive actions state exactly what is removed and what is preserved. Long lists scroll with focus so every row remains reachable without a mouse."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "rKEDe",
      "x": -820,
      "y": -2600,
      "name": "note · 10-foot scale",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "10-FOOT SCALE\n• The design target is 1920×1080 and viewing from television distance.\n• Base UI text is 22 px with an 18 px minimum. Dim text against the window background must retain accessible contrast at its rendered size.\n• Display text uses Khand 600 in uppercase with 0.03em tracking; UI text uses IBM Plex Sans; technical values use IBM Plex Mono.\n• Controls use 40, 48, and 56 px heights with targets of at least 48 px. Focus is always visible through a 3 px accent ring plus an accent-tinted background.\n• Layout respects a 96 px horizontal and 54 px vertical safe area."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "8ihsE",
      "x": -1650,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "note 00 · 10-foot shell",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "00 · 10-FOOT SHELL\n• The 1920×1080 window uses one 96 px top bar and one 72 px button-hint footer.\n• Primary navigation contains exactly Home, Library, and Settings. Previous/next-section controls never wrap at the ends.\n• Directional input stays inside the active page. Back moves up one level and asks for confirmation before leaving Home; it never closes the application unexpectedly.\n• Focus is persistent per section, restored on return, and automatically scrolled into view.\n• Mouse, keyboard, and controller input expose the same actions and enabled states.\n• The top bar shows product identity and local status only; CE has no account-dependent navigation."
    },
